VEDAS Signatures
================

The detection content in this repository is generated and curated by
ARPSyndicate's Vulnerability & Exploit Data Aggregation System (VEDAS).

This work is only possible because of the open security ecosystem. VEDAS
aggregates publicly available intelligence (OSINT) from across the internet —
vulnerability databases and advisories, exploit and proof-of-concept
publications, detection rulesets, security research, blog posts, and the
countless disclosures shared by vendors, CERTs, independent researchers, and
the wider cybersecurity community. The signatures here stand on that collective
body of knowledge, and we gratefully acknowledge everyone who contributes to it.

Where specific detection logic (request paths, parameters, matchers) was adapted
from an openly licensed project, we credit it explicitly. In particular, some
Nuclei templates were informed by the open-source project:

  projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates  —  https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates
  Copyright (c) ProjectDiscovery, Inc.  —  MIT License

Community contributions to this repository are credited to their authors in the
`info.author` field of the templates they submit and in the pull-request history.

If you believe your work should be attributed here, please open an issue.
